-- title:
--   Finite preprocessing program for the terminal embedding
-- statement:
--   This fixed 1386-instruction program receives the terminal coordinates, $\varepsilon$ and $S$. It computes an ordered Gram–Schmidt basis of the terminal span, terminal coordinates and distances, every ordered empirical test, and the deterministic sign projection; it stores the terminal images $b_i$. Zero residuals are dropped during basis construction and zero empirical averages are omitted before normalization. No separation or generic-position hypothesis is part of the input. The dimension counter stops at the first integer $m\ge1$ for which
--
--   $$\exp(mS(\varepsilon/6)^4/512)\ge32n(n-1).$$
--
--   Thus parameter selection uses the source's primitives. The singleton branch stores final dimension one. The output memory is the common persistent state for all queries, with no correctness or runtime certificate stored in it.
-- source:
--   Vladimir Braverman, Kuan Cheng, Jiaqing Zhu, STOC 2027 submission #1373 (October 2026), pp. 20–22, Theorem 1.1, equations (38)–(44), preprocessing bound (48); https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-2/1373.pdf

